e you much more likely to go to if  you choose the second dentist it's not  because of the  service or the product because it's the  same you end up with the same kind of  teeth cleaning  you're choosing the why they do it  because they treat you like family  my husband and i have never used social  media to promote our business and we  have had several millionaire clients  just through word of mouth alone and i  know that we're not the only ones  ginza george has never had social media  to leverage her hospitality business and  it's worked out well for her  dr cal newport has never had social  media in his life and he's a successful  computer scientist  speaker and author i do not disagree  that social media can help  leverage the advertising of your  business but if avoiding social media is  something that you want to do  know that you don't have to have it in  order to promote your business  the first thing that i would recommend  to you if having a business without  social media is something that you want  to do  is know that your reputation is huge  so make sure to have a clearly defined  why for what you're doing what you're  doing  so that your clients or your customers  can know that through your service  but aside from all of that know that  there are other means that you can use  to get the word out such as attending  networking events  or conferences using email lists or  producing  content online such as courses or  youtube videos  and if you yourself have a business but  don't have social media  share your ideas in the comments i  assure you that there are other people  that are asking the same question  the next question is how will i buy or  sell my stuff  i am almost going on six years now  without social media so i was totally  oblivious to the fact that you can sell  on websites like facebook i had no idea  but when i moved i actually sold and  donated a lot of items  through several different things that i  did the first and probably the simplest  word of mouth my job has a flyer where  you can post things that you're selling  and i know that certain newspapers have  this availability as well  but i also posted pictures in the break  room of certain things that i was  selling  when it came to selling to people that i  knew i had to be mindful  of who i thought could benefit from that  particular item for example  i had a traction device that did not  work for me or my husband it  pulled on his hernia and i hated the  feeling of blood going up to my head  so i did have a friend that had back  problems she had mentioned that to me  before so when i talked to her about  this  device she was so happy to have the deal  there are numerous ways that you can  sell your items  you can do yard sales you can do  consignment sales as well which is  something that i've done  before like clothing if you intend to  donate it or get rid of it anyway  go to consignment shops and they will  actually buy your clothes that are  gently used  or you can use apps like let go which is  something that i personally used  i mean you don't need facebook for this  the next question is  how will i stay in touch with people i  actually talk about this a little bit in  my video on why i quit social media so  i'm not going to go too much into detail  to drag this video on  but the main point that i want to make  is to focus on making connections with  the people in your life  for example if your friend nancy tells  you that she has a job interview in two  weeks  schedule it in your calendar to remember  to call her either beforehand to give  her encouragement  or afterwards to see how it went be  intentional and remember to do this  i actually schedule birthdays on my  phone to remember to call people  and especially keep in touch with  friends or family that are going through  rough times  maybe others haven't done this for you  maybe when you had a surgery or you were  sick  everybody forgot all about you okay so  you know how it feels  don't be that person too be the friend  that cares and is there when it matters  most  when you focus on making deeper  connections and improving the  relationships that you value  you won't feel that need to have  hundreds of superficial friendships and  comments and likes  the next question what if i lose my  friends  i'm gonna give you the cold hard truth  be prepared that you will  likely lose some friends but i'll give  you a secret  these are just friends that you thought  you had that's okay  it's a good thing about 10 years ago my  husband had a great job where he was  making lots of money  but he spent it all on hosting parties  with free alcohol  and if his buddies needed cash for some  reason he would give it to them  not ever really expecting it back as you  can imagine he had lots of friends  during this time  but when he was rear-ended lost his job  because he wasn't able to work anymore  ended up in a wheelchair and doctors  told him that he was never going to walk  again  because of his back injury only four  friends ever visited him or called him  up to see how he was doing  and those friends that he had helped out  when they needed money  guess where they were when he had lost  his job and he had thousands to pay in  medical bills  who knows they never showed up so what  do i mean by all of this  is the quantity of friends does not  matter nearly as much as the quality  of your friendships when this happened  to him he didn't really  lose friends because they weren't  friends to begin with the weeds just  remove themselves  you don't need weeds in your life you  want people in your life that actually  care about you  people that motivate you to be better or  people that you'd like to learn  something from or that you'd like to be  more like  people that inspire you to be a better  version of yourself keep in touch with  these people  because the rest they're just weeds the  next question is  how will i meet new people okay first of  all there's more than one way to catch a  rabbit  but if you want to meet new people the  first thing that you have to do  is to actually be open to it i mean when  you go to the grocery store don't just  mindlessly stare at your phone or the  magazines at checkout actually smile and  talk to the person behind you  but also make it a point to attend  events where the people that you would  like to meet would likely be at  if you want to make friends that are  focused on the same business goals as  you you might find them at a conference  or networking event if you want friends  of the same faith you might find them at  events at your church  my brother for example corvette dude who  has a corvette and a maserati  loves to talk about cars so he finds  people that have the same interests and  hobbies  at car shows so ask yourself what kind  of people you want to meet in the first  place  and that will lead you to your answer  but before we continue  i have a question for you what do you  think about online dating  do people really get to know each other  on social media what are your thoughts  let me know in the comments the next  question is  what do i do when i'm bored i actually  find this one kind of funny now because  it reminds me of when i  initially quit and how i thought the  world had just ended because i didn't  know what i was going to do with myself  now  this one comes down to one thing habits  your use of social media is a habit when  you quit cold turkey your brain is  stressed out because  now this ritual this habit that you once  did is now gone and there's a void that  it has to fill  and a lot of times this is the reason  that people cave in and they go back to  the habit they tried to kick in the  first place  so you attack this the same way that you  would any other habit and there's lots  of things that you can do  to adopt positive habits and to remove  negative habits  so i'm just gonna share three quick tips  with you tip number one  make it pleasurable quitting social  media can initially leave you with  withdrawal symptoms  so make yourself happy that it's gone by  rewarding yourself  or distracting yourself with happy  things maybe go back to that hobby that  you once had  take a walk in nature exercise take this  time for self-care  or to spend more time with friends and  family take this extra time to invest in  yourself so that you can become a better  version of yourself  instead of reading about other people's  lives or posting all about your life  make your life better tip number two  make it difficult  make it harder to go back by deleting  the apps and getting rid of the accounts  and cut out the triggers that normally  make you go there in the first place  for example if you normally scroll  through social media when you go to bed  then maybe consider placing your phone  across the room or perhaps even better  in another room  or turning your phone off before you go  to bed if your trigger is normally to  pull your phone out and scroll through  social media anytime you have down time  such as for example waiting at a  doctor's office  consider turning your phone off and  taking a book with you instead  and tip number three make yourself  accountable  consider letting the friends know that  we'll actually support you in this  and maybe challenging someone to do it  along with you  or maybe even make it a little bit  better by making there a negative  consequence  if you do go back for example when i put  sodas several years ago i made a bet  with my sister  i told her that if she saw me take even  just one sip of soda  in six months she would get fifty  dollars  this gave me an even bigger incentive to  not go back to that habit these are only  a few tips but for  greater detail on developing or cutting  out habits i  highly highly recommend the book atomic  habits  this is actually a book that i've read a  few times over the years because it's  one that's  easily applicable to any kind of habit  whether you're trying to adopt new  healthier habits such as  exercising reading or eating healthier  or if you're trying to cut off  negative habits that are harmful for you  this book can be a huge help  i'll leave the link in the description  and last but definitely not least i want  to address the biggest  fear that you guys mentioned in the  comments and that is fomo  i think there's a huge deal of fear of  missing out on social media because it's  designed to keep you addicted  there's just something about the ability  to infinitely scroll in those  darn little notifications that you just  want to tap on  because you have to see what it's all  about  at least for me i definitely experience  withdrawal within the first few weeks  but i think that it does  all come down to habits it had become a  habit of mine to  constantly check on the messages check  on the likes scroll through posts  what if i was missing out on something  and once it was gone it was like i had  nothing else to think about but what i  was missing  guys this is short term that feeling  goes away once you get  used to that old habit being gone but  it's a million times easier if you shift  your focus from what you're missing out  on  to what you're gaining you have all this  extra time now think about all the  things that you can do to make your life  better so don't focus on what you're  missing out on focus on  adding more activities that will help  you improve your life get back to those  hobbies you love or adopt new hobbies  love the people in your life and live  fully when you're living a life you love  you will not have time to miss those  apps this list of questions is by no  means exhaustive and i probably missed  several points so if you guys have other  suggestions or ideas  please share them in the comments  because there are other people asking  what do i do that is it for today guys  if you like this video please give it a  thumbs up and subscribe so that you  won't miss out on my videos  i thank you so much for watching and i  can't wait to see you in the next one

